@@ -17,6 +17,25 @@ The base fixture uses Python standard library components only:
 
 The base intentionally contains the pre-treatment state for S01/S02/S04. Evaluator self-tests must prove those scenarios are red-capable while public baseline tests remain green.
 
+## Pausing Jobs
+
+`POST /api/jobs/{id}/pause` pauses scheduling and
+`POST /api/jobs/{id}/resume` resumes it. Both accept an empty body and return
+HTTP 200 with the updated `{"job": ...}` object. Repeating either request is
+safe; an unknown Job returns the existing HTTP 404 error format.
+
+Jobs expose a `paused` boolean through the API and a Paused column on the
+dashboard. New and existing Jobs default to unpaused. Pause state persists in
+the Store database, including databases created before this feature.
+
+A paused Job rejects new scheduled Runs with HTTP 409. Manual Runs remain
+allowed. Existing Runs continue with their normal Attempts, retries, outcomes,
+and alerts. Pausing preserves the independent enabled setting; resuming a
+disabled Job leaves it disabled. Updating enabled does not clear a pause.
+The dashboard continues to display the last completed Run result while paused.
+
+Verify with `python -m unittest discover -s tests -v`.
+
 ## Pilot scope
 
 The first implementation slice supports only:
